1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:00,972
Friday,

2
00:00:00,972 --> 00:00:02,052
four forty five.

3
00:00:02,052 --> 00:00:04,279
A developer fixes one tiny thing,

4
00:00:04,279 --> 00:00:05,629
a greater than sign,

5
00:00:05,629 --> 00:00:07,113
and pushes the change.

6
00:00:07,663 --> 00:00:09,061
The pipeline is green.

7
00:00:09,061 --> 00:00:10,269
Everything deploys.

8
00:00:10,269 --> 00:00:11,158
And on Monday,

9
00:00:11,158 --> 00:00:13,573
customers cannot see a single product.

10
00:00:14,123 --> 00:00:17,826
Nothing in the pipeline asked the application a real question.

11
00:00:17,826 --> 00:00:19,319
Nothing stopped the line.

12
00:00:19,319 --> 00:00:21,589
And nobody could go back in one click.

13
00:00:22,139 --> 00:00:23,614
Today we fix all three.

14
00:00:23,614 --> 00:00:25,410
Gates that stop a bad build.

15
00:00:25,410 --> 00:00:27,013
Secrets that stay secret.

16
00:00:27,013 --> 00:00:31,629
A release that switches traffic only when the new version proves itself,

17
00:00:31,629 --> 00:00:33,297
and rolls back in seconds.

18
00:00:33,847 --> 00:00:39,287
Real Jenkins, real Nexus, real Tomcat, and a real router. Deploy without fear.

19
00:00:40,837 --> 00:00:42,266
Here is what to expect.

20
00:00:42,816 --> 00:00:43,533
One: gates.

21
00:00:43,533 --> 00:00:46,855
How a pipeline refuses to move a bad build forward,

22
00:00:46,855 --> 00:00:48,875
and where a human must say yes.

23
00:00:49,425 --> 00:00:54,545
Two: secrets and least privilege. Where a password lives, and what a stolen one can do.

24
00:00:55,095 --> 00:00:59,852
Three: release strategies. Rolling, blue green, and canary, and how to go back.

25
00:01:00,402 --> 00:01:04,328
Four: verification. A smoke test, and a message to the team.

26
00:01:04,878 --> 00:01:06,413
Then we run all of it,

27
00:01:06,413 --> 00:01:06,762
live.

28
00:01:06,762 --> 00:01:12,067
This lesson covers objectives four to seven of the CI CD Engineering domain.

29
00:01:13,617 --> 00:01:17,329
First, gates. A gate is a place where the pipeline can say no.

30
00:01:17,879 --> 00:01:19,993
The first gate is the test gate.

31
00:01:19,993 --> 00:01:21,182
If one test fails,

32
00:01:21,182 --> 00:01:22,305
the stage is red,

33
00:01:22,305 --> 00:01:24,683
and every stage after it is skipped.

34
00:01:24,683 --> 00:01:27,458
Nothing broken gets published or deployed.

35
00:01:28,008 --> 00:01:29,864
The second is a quality gate.

36
00:01:29,864 --> 00:01:32,680
A tool such as sonar cube measures the code,

37
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:35,432
and the pipeline fails when coverage drops,

38
00:01:35,432 --> 00:01:36,648
or new bugs appear.

39
00:01:37,198 --> 00:01:38,957
The third is a human gate.

40
00:01:38,957 --> 00:01:40,175
A manual approval,

41
00:01:40,175 --> 00:01:41,393
before production.

42
00:01:41,393 --> 00:01:42,747
The pipeline pauses,

43
00:01:42,747 --> 00:01:43,897
shows a question,

44
00:01:43,897 --> 00:01:45,454
and waits for a person.

45
00:01:46,004 --> 00:01:49,350
Use automatic gates for anything a machine can judge,

46
00:01:49,350 --> 00:01:52,443
and a human gate for risk a machine cannot judge.

47
00:01:52,443 --> 00:01:55,284
And always keep the log of who approved what.

48
00:01:56,834 --> 00:02:00,823
Second, secrets. A secret is a password, a token, or a key.

49
00:02:01,373 --> 00:02:03,976
Rule one: a secret never goes into Git.

50
00:02:03,976 --> 00:02:05,644
Not in the pipeline file,

51
00:02:05,644 --> 00:02:06,712
not in a script,

52
00:02:06,712 --> 00:02:08,247
not in a settings file.

53
00:02:08,247 --> 00:02:09,715
Git remembers forever.

54
00:02:10,265 --> 00:02:12,968
Rule two: the secret lives in one place,

55
00:02:12,968 --> 00:02:14,319
Jenkins credentials.

56
00:02:14,319 --> 00:02:16,550
The pipeline asks for it by name,

57
00:02:16,550 --> 00:02:19,929
and Jenkins hands it over only while the job runs.

58
00:02:20,479 --> 00:02:23,358
Rule three: if the secret appears in a log,

59
00:02:23,358 --> 00:02:25,770
Jenkins replaces it with four stars.

60
00:02:25,770 --> 00:02:27,243
But do not rely on it.

61
00:02:27,243 --> 00:02:28,649
Never print a secret.

62
00:02:29,199 --> 00:02:30,989
Rule four: least privilege.

63
00:02:30,989 --> 00:02:33,706
The deploy identity can upload a release.

64
00:02:33,706 --> 00:02:35,098
It cannot delete one.

65
00:02:35,098 --> 00:02:36,556
If its password leaks,

66
00:02:36,556 --> 00:02:37,882
the damage is small.

67
00:02:39,432 --> 00:02:43,336
Third, how a new version reaches users. Three common strategies.

68
00:02:43,886 --> 00:02:44,407
Rolling.

69
00:02:44,407 --> 00:02:46,359
Replace servers one at a time.

70
00:02:46,359 --> 00:02:46,749
Cheap,

71
00:02:46,749 --> 00:02:47,790
but for a while,

72
00:02:47,790 --> 00:02:49,417
old and new run together,

73
00:02:49,417 --> 00:02:51,694
and going back means rolling again.

74
00:02:52,244 --> 00:02:52,970
Blue green.

75
00:02:52,970 --> 00:02:55,016
Two identical production sides.

76
00:02:55,016 --> 00:02:56,204
Users are on blue.

77
00:02:56,204 --> 00:02:58,581
You deploy the new version to green,

78
00:02:58,581 --> 00:03:00,033
test it with no users,

79
00:03:00,033 --> 00:03:01,815
and then switch the router.

80
00:03:01,815 --> 00:03:03,465
Going back is one switch.

81
00:03:04,015 --> 00:03:04,482
Canary.

82
00:03:04,482 --> 00:03:06,349
Send a small slice of users,

83
00:03:06,349 --> 00:03:07,215
five percent,

84
00:03:07,215 --> 00:03:08,482
to the new version.

85
00:03:08,482 --> 00:03:09,615
Watch the errors.

86
00:03:09,615 --> 00:03:10,949
Then grow the slice,

87
00:03:10,949 --> 00:03:11,482
or stop.

88
00:03:12,032 --> 00:03:12,864
And rollback.

89
00:03:12,864 --> 00:03:15,040
Because Nexus keeps every version,

90
00:03:15,040 --> 00:03:16,704
rollback is not a rebuild.

91
00:03:16,704 --> 00:03:20,224
It is a promotion of an older file that already worked.

92
00:03:20,774 --> 00:03:24,742
In the demo we use blue green, because it shows the idea most clearly.

93
00:03:26,292 --> 00:03:30,985
Fourth, verification. A green deploy only means the file was copied.

94
00:03:31,535 --> 00:03:35,532
A smoke test asks the running application a few real questions.

95
00:03:35,532 --> 00:03:37,626
Is the version the one we expect?

96
00:03:37,626 --> 00:03:39,276
Does the home page answer?

97
00:03:39,276 --> 00:03:41,115
Does the product list answer?

98
00:03:41,115 --> 00:03:42,575
If any answer is wrong,

99
00:03:42,575 --> 00:03:43,717
the release stops.

100
00:03:44,267 --> 00:03:45,812
Keep it small and fast.

101
00:03:45,812 --> 00:03:48,364
A smoke test is not a full test suite.

102
00:03:48,364 --> 00:03:51,051
It is the question: is anything on fire?

103
00:03:51,601 --> 00:03:52,665
And tell people.

104
00:03:52,665 --> 00:03:53,662
A notification,

105
00:03:53,662 --> 00:03:54,793
in chat or email,

106
00:03:54,793 --> 00:03:55,924
with the version,

107
00:03:55,924 --> 00:03:56,655
the result,

108
00:03:56,655 --> 00:03:58,252
and a link to the build.

109
00:03:58,252 --> 00:04:01,777
A failure nobody hears about is a failure that lasts.

110
00:04:03,327 --> 00:04:04,241
Same Jenkins,

111
00:04:04,241 --> 00:04:05,226
same two jobs.

112
00:04:05,226 --> 00:04:07,617
The pipeline has a new last stage,

113
00:04:07,617 --> 00:04:08,531
a smoke test,

114
00:04:08,531 --> 00:04:11,696
and the promote job now has an approval step.

115
00:04:11,696 --> 00:04:15,423
Production is serving version one point oh point one.

116
00:04:15,973 --> 00:04:16,317
First,

117
00:04:16,317 --> 00:04:17,064
the terminal.

118
00:04:17,064 --> 00:04:19,475
Production is reached through one address,

119
00:04:19,475 --> 00:04:20,106
the router.

120
00:04:20,106 --> 00:04:21,541
We ask it for its health.

121
00:04:22,091 --> 00:04:26,699
Version one point oh point one. The router file says where it sends the traffic.

122
00:04:27,249 --> 00:04:32,241
Port ninety one oh three, and the comment says blue. Blue is serving users. And green?

123
00:04:33,891 --> 00:04:35,512
Empty. Green is waiting.

124
00:04:36,062 --> 00:04:38,281
Now a developer tidies the shipping rule.

125
00:04:41,431 --> 00:04:45,186
One symbol changed. Greater than or equal, became greater than.

126
00:04:45,736 --> 00:04:48,232
It looks harmless. The developer commits it.

127
00:04:50,182 --> 00:04:52,870
In Jenkins, we open Cloud Cart CI.

128
00:04:56,720 --> 00:04:57,893
And click Build Now.

129
00:05:00,543 --> 00:05:02,058
We open the stages view.

130
00:05:06,808 --> 00:05:08,087
The pipeline runs.

131
00:05:08,087 --> 00:05:09,081
Secrets check,

132
00:05:09,081 --> 00:05:09,650
version,

133
00:05:09,650 --> 00:05:11,355
and then build and test.

134
00:05:11,355 --> 00:05:11,640
Red.

135
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:13,203
The line stopped here.

136
00:05:13,203 --> 00:05:13,771
Publish,

137
00:05:13,771 --> 00:05:16,045
deploy and smoke test never ran.

138
00:05:24,295 --> 00:05:26,236
We open the console, to see why.

139
00:05:31,086 --> 00:05:32,076
One test failed,

140
00:05:32,076 --> 00:05:32,571
by name.

141
00:05:32,571 --> 00:05:34,490
Free shipping at the threshold.

142
00:05:34,490 --> 00:05:37,955
The old rule gave free shipping at exactly seventy five.

143
00:05:37,955 --> 00:05:39,255
The new one does not.

144
00:05:39,255 --> 00:05:40,430
The gate caught it.

145
00:05:40,980 --> 00:05:43,732
Back in the terminal, the team has already been told.

146
00:05:45,382 --> 00:05:48,797
Version one point oh point two was never published.

147
00:05:48,797 --> 00:05:50,805
Nexus has nothing to clean up,

148
00:05:50,805 --> 00:05:52,211
and dev is untouched.

149
00:05:52,211 --> 00:05:53,617
We revert the change.

150
00:05:54,167 --> 00:05:56,066
In Jenkins, Build Now again.

151
00:05:59,516 --> 00:06:01,030
We open the stages view.

152
00:06:05,580 --> 00:06:06,724
Green all the way,

153
00:06:06,724 --> 00:06:08,566
including the new smoke test.

154
00:06:08,566 --> 00:06:10,663
Version one point oh point three.

155
00:06:10,663 --> 00:06:12,124
The number two is gone,

156
00:06:12,124 --> 00:06:13,204
and that is fine.

157
00:06:13,204 --> 00:06:14,284
Numbers are free.

158
00:06:42,434 --> 00:06:43,736
We open the console.

159
00:06:49,386 --> 00:06:53,332
Smoke test, passed. The application answered all three questions.

160
00:06:53,882 --> 00:06:54,633
Now secrets.

161
00:06:54,633 --> 00:06:56,261
At the top of the console,

162
00:06:56,261 --> 00:06:57,450
in the first stage,

163
00:06:57,450 --> 00:06:59,578
I printed the password on purpose.

164
00:07:00,128 --> 00:07:05,632
Jenkins replaced it with four stars. A safety net, not a plan. Never print a secret.

165
00:07:06,182 --> 00:07:10,001
Where does the real password live? In Jenkins, under Credentials.

166
00:07:15,051 --> 00:07:18,934
One entry, nexus deployer. The pipeline asks for it by name.

167
00:07:19,484 --> 00:07:24,006
And what can this identity do? It can upload. Can it delete a release? We try.

168
00:07:27,356 --> 00:07:32,455
Four oh three. Forbidden. A leaked deployer password cannot erase your releases.

169
00:07:33,005 --> 00:07:35,586
Now production. We open the promote job.

170
00:07:39,936 --> 00:07:41,238
Build with Parameters.

171
00:07:44,788 --> 00:07:46,601
Version one point oh point three.

172
00:07:48,351 --> 00:07:49,418
Target, prod.

173
00:07:52,168 --> 00:07:52,978
And Build.

174
00:07:55,928 --> 00:07:57,443
We open the stages view.

175
00:08:03,893 --> 00:08:05,170
The pipeline stops,

176
00:08:05,170 --> 00:08:05,841
and waits.

177
00:08:05,841 --> 00:08:06,446
Approval.

178
00:08:06,446 --> 00:08:07,991
This is the human gate.

179
00:08:07,991 --> 00:08:09,738
The question is on screen.

180
00:08:10,288 --> 00:08:11,974
We decide yes. Release.

181
00:08:13,824 --> 00:08:18,005
Now the release runs. Blue green. First, the idle side, green.

182
00:08:18,555 --> 00:08:19,856
We open the console.

183
00:08:24,706 --> 00:08:26,324
Green gets the new version,

184
00:08:26,324 --> 00:08:28,302
and the smoke test runs on green,

185
00:08:28,302 --> 00:08:30,040
before any user can reach it.

186
00:08:34,290 --> 00:08:36,786
It passes. Only now the router switches.

187
00:08:37,336 --> 00:08:38,122
And once more,

188
00:08:38,122 --> 00:08:38,965
the smoke test,

189
00:08:38,965 --> 00:08:40,032
through the router,

190
00:08:40,032 --> 00:08:42,392
to prove that users reach the new version.

191
00:08:42,942 --> 00:08:45,267
In the terminal, production, through the router.

192
00:08:47,617 --> 00:08:50,220
One point oh point three. And the two sides?

193
00:08:50,770 --> 00:08:56,188
Blue still runs one point oh point one. That is the instant rollback, one switch away.

194
00:08:56,738 --> 00:09:00,344
Now the bad release. An engineer renames the API path.

195
00:09:02,594 --> 00:09:06,092
The change is small, and the unit tests do not look at web paths.

196
00:09:06,642 --> 00:09:07,325
Commit.

197
00:09:10,575 --> 00:09:12,004
Jenkins, Build Now.

198
00:09:15,854 --> 00:09:17,049
The stages view.

199
00:09:21,499 --> 00:09:27,195
Everything is green. Build, tests, publish, deploy to dev. And then, the smoke test. Red.

200
00:09:55,045 --> 00:09:55,962
The console.

201
00:10:01,512 --> 00:10:02,821
The health is right.

202
00:10:02,821 --> 00:10:04,260
The home page answers.

203
00:10:04,260 --> 00:10:06,812
But the product list says four oh four.

204
00:10:06,812 --> 00:10:09,428
A real customer would see an empty shop.

205
00:10:09,428 --> 00:10:11,326
Only a smoke test finds this.

206
00:10:11,876 --> 00:10:13,113
And the team is told.

207
00:10:16,363 --> 00:10:19,688
Now imagine someone pushes it to production anyway.

208
00:10:19,688 --> 00:10:20,731
The promote job.

209
00:10:20,731 --> 00:10:22,166
Build with Parameters.

210
00:10:26,616 --> 00:10:28,472
Version one point oh point four.

211
00:10:30,122 --> 00:10:31,188
Target, prod.

212
00:10:33,938 --> 00:10:34,664
Build.

213
00:10:37,814 --> 00:10:40,864
We open the stages view, and the approval is waiting.

214
00:10:45,814 --> 00:10:48,694
A human says yes, hoping for the best. Release.

215
00:10:50,744 --> 00:10:53,155
The release runs. This time, the console.

216
00:10:58,105 --> 00:11:03,566
The smoke test fails on the idle side. The router never switched. Traffic stays on green.

217
00:11:08,216 --> 00:11:10,563
In the terminal, production is still healthy.

218
00:11:12,813 --> 00:11:17,933
Users never saw version one point oh point four. That is the value of blue green.

219
00:11:18,483 --> 00:11:19,331
Now rollback.

220
00:11:19,331 --> 00:11:22,072
Suppose a problem appears after a release.

221
00:11:22,072 --> 00:11:23,834
We do not rebuild anything.

222
00:11:23,834 --> 00:11:26,966
We promote an older version that already worked.

223
00:11:26,966 --> 00:11:28,467
One point oh point one.

224
00:11:29,017 --> 00:11:31,428
The same job. Build with Parameters.

225
00:11:34,578 --> 00:11:36,348
Version one point oh point one.

226
00:11:38,198 --> 00:11:39,265
Target, prod.

227
00:11:42,015 --> 00:11:42,740
Build.

228
00:11:45,890 --> 00:11:48,344
We open the stages view, and the approval.

229
00:11:53,994 --> 00:11:55,338
We approve. Release.

230
00:11:56,788 --> 00:11:57,832
The release runs.

231
00:11:57,832 --> 00:11:59,922
Blue gets the old file from Nexus,

232
00:11:59,922 --> 00:12:01,397
the checksum is checked,

233
00:12:01,397 --> 00:12:02,749
the smoke test passes,

234
00:12:02,749 --> 00:12:04,532
and the router switches back.

235
00:12:06,882 --> 00:12:10,935
In the terminal. Production, through the router. One point oh point one.

236
00:12:11,485 --> 00:12:12,664
That is a rollback,

237
00:12:12,664 --> 00:12:13,781
in about a minute.

238
00:12:13,781 --> 00:12:14,464
No rebuild,

239
00:12:14,464 --> 00:12:15,209
no guessing,

240
00:12:15,209 --> 00:12:17,629
and the same safe steps as any release.

241
00:12:19,179 --> 00:12:20,182
Let us recap.

242
00:12:20,732 --> 00:12:21,109
Gates.

243
00:12:21,109 --> 00:12:24,441
Tests and quality checks stop the line automatically.

244
00:12:24,441 --> 00:12:26,641
A human approval guards production.

245
00:12:27,191 --> 00:12:27,750
Secrets.

246
00:12:27,750 --> 00:12:29,358
In Jenkins credentials,

247
00:12:29,358 --> 00:12:30,267
never in Git,

248
00:12:30,267 --> 00:12:31,245
never printed,

249
00:12:31,245 --> 00:12:33,762
and a deployer that can only upload.

250
00:12:34,312 --> 00:12:34,877
Releases.

251
00:12:34,877 --> 00:12:38,333
Blue green tested the new version before users arrived,

252
00:12:38,333 --> 00:12:41,224
and rollback was a promotion of an older file.

253
00:12:41,774 --> 00:12:47,448
Verification. A smoke test asks real questions, and a notification tells the team.

254
00:12:47,998 --> 00:12:48,717
Next lesson,

255
00:12:48,717 --> 00:12:49,675
the mastery lab.

256
00:12:49,675 --> 00:12:51,113
We measure the pipeline,

257
00:12:51,113 --> 00:12:52,430
troubleshoot failures,

258
00:12:52,430 --> 00:12:54,526
and prove everything independently.

259
00:12:56,076 --> 00:12:58,167
Your turn. On your own machine only.

260
00:12:58,717 --> 00:13:02,215
One. Break a unit test on purpose, and watch the line stop.

261
00:13:02,765 --> 00:13:03,010
Two.

262
00:13:03,010 --> 00:13:06,613
Move a password out of a file and into Jenkins credentials.

263
00:13:06,613 --> 00:13:07,469
Then print it,

264
00:13:07,469 --> 00:13:08,568
and see the stars.

265
00:13:09,118 --> 00:13:13,790
Three. Add a smoke test with three questions, and a notification when it fails.

266
00:13:14,340 --> 00:13:19,161
Four. Add an approval step before production, and a second side for blue green.

267
00:13:19,711 --> 00:13:22,293
Pause the video, and do it before you continue.

268
00:13:37,843 --> 00:13:39,486
Quick check. Answer aloud.

269
00:13:40,036 --> 00:13:43,556
Which gates stop a build automatically, and which needs a person?

270
00:13:44,106 --> 00:13:47,754
Why must a secret never be printed, even if Jenkins hides it?

271
00:13:48,304 --> 00:13:50,842
Why does blue green make rollback so fast?

272
00:13:51,392 --> 00:13:54,358
Why is a green deploy not proof that the release works?

273
00:14:04,908 --> 00:14:06,883
If you found this lesson useful,

274
00:14:06,883 --> 00:14:07,623
please like,

275
00:14:07,623 --> 00:14:07,994
share,

